{"id": "EUVD-2026-86228", "enisaUuid": "d9af75f8-6faa-3d33-9bc2-495c67f90974", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nphy: fsl-imx8mq-usb: fix typec switch leak on probe error path\n\nIf probe fails after imx95_usb_phy_get_tca() succeeds, the typec\nswitch leaks because the only cleanup path was in .remove(), which\nnever runs on probe failure.\n\nUse devm_add_action_or_reset() so the switch is cleaned up on both\nprobe failure and driver removal. The imx95_usb_phy_put_tca() is no\nlonger needed, it will be removed in .remove() too.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:21:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:07:36", "baseScore": 7.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f1b7b2c7ffa9711d1298f52790b377fe02efc1db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/84646f5b945a370f6999eed59a334387b0abc282", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/87a1805b1c346b092c34f96f3806f207792910e1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93225", "GHSA-x24p-xpmf-j8m7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "145c5fe8-f037-3e07-a37f-17c6def5346a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "4802d68d-91e4-3082-ace6-a8c0338d2513", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "487c776a-9691-3fe6-80ce-5cbc481c908d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b58f0f86fd6156d7b084257f5c91ceaf7d760927 <87a1805b1c346b092c34f96f3806f207792910e1"}, {"id": "4c5a0fec-df00-3a75-8b19-622f5e774761", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "673dac4b-d81f-3062-b2cf-332a90c61abb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b58f0f86fd6156d7b084257f5c91ceaf7d760927 <84646f5b945a370f6999eed59a334387b0abc282"}, {"id": "cef97d46-bc10-3ccf-